    "body": "Make runner-owned EventStore package integration blocking after all twenty isolated projects pass, using the exact published CLI 4.44.0/Builds 6249 v2 producer and the qualified additional Tenants owner. Preserve the real gateway readiness/persisted Redis end-state and anonymous-status assertions, owned test harness and exact cleanup; record native diagnostics from the existing scrubbed descriptor/plan/source-mapping handoff.\n\nThe latest correction changes only the direct Platform gitlink and docs/ci.md: adopt published Platform 1.2.3/source991e2df97dc8493e41096006b0d3203a71730ae8. Its incoming Tenants API app-channel alias correction preserves distinct application-channel and Dapr API credentials. Direct Builds 6249/CLI 4.44.0/v2 ref6249, Tenants 1b2, all workflow/native/declaration/harness bytes, all independent jobs and the 600-second startup bound are unchanged. Platform's source-bound 201-case tuple and 60-case SDK matrix are component evidence, not a native reference pass.\n\nValidation at b63dc2fe15e41621741d0e49e088f10046ec7bed:\n\n- Normal package preparation with the genuine signed 4.44.0 archive, exact version/source and existing official Tenants 7 cache passed; offline repository signature and archive SHA256 verified.\n- Contracts Release/package build passed with 0 warnings/errors. All 5 focused caller/harness tests executed/passed with 0 skips; actual TRX retained.\n- Released owner-selection controls 3/3, actual CLI/manifest checks, actionlint, whitespace and owning locked 21.2.4 complete commit/title validation passed. All 44 protected input hashes match 005c; no nested dependencies initialized.\n\nPrior 005c CI 41787766444/attempt1 remains a genuine failure: all 20 isolated reports executed 16,160 passes/0 failed/49 NotExecuted and all 5 independent jobs passed, then required native startup timed out with HXR021 at 600 seconds. Gateway/domain were unhealthy and API had exited; native Facts never ran. Actual detailed API exit text was not retained, so no exact hosted root-cause log is claimed. Exact cleanup verified 10 owned names removed, no remaining inventories/discovery uncertainty, and preserved the first startup-timeout. The public 4.44.0 helper's separate lifecycle-body retention gap remains unresolved by this dependency-only update.\n\nThe normal new-head pipeline must now complete all unchanged isolated/independent gates, both real native Facts and exact cleanup/artifact verification. No unchanged 005c rerun, skipped job, increased timeout, provider credential, registry mutation, source bypass, release or candidate acceptance. Corrected Builds publication/coherent later adoption, full Parties qualification and manual cancellation/lifecycle evidence remain separate pending story requirements.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes CI evidence retention and strict handoff validation for native integration; incorrect binding or I/O behavior could fail or skew hosted qualification without affecting production runtime paths.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Adds **runner-owned native diagnostics** for the `platform-package` integration suite: after gateway/Redis persistence checks pass, tests emit bounded JSON of **assemblies loaded in the test process** (Hexalith.* + StackExchange.Redis), bound to the published G4 handoff (descriptor, plan, mapping hash, caller Git revision). On **Linux CI**, observations are written once under `TestResults/module-integration` with symlink/overwrite guards; locally they stay on the TRX channel only.\n> \n> New **`NativeDiagnosticBinding`** validates executor env vars and cross-document consistency before retention; unit tests cover handoff refusals and file I/O boundaries. **`GatewayPersistenceTests`** takes `ITestOutputHelper` and invokes the writer after assertions.\n> \n> **`docs/ci.md`** documents the diagnostic contract and states that prior hosted runs (startup timeout / missing native TRX bodies) do **not** qualify this merge—fresh CI must prove retained diagnostics and native facts.\n> \n> **Contracts packaging tests** now require `integration-test-reference-owners: tenants` in shared CI v2 wiring and assert the semantic-release governance job is blocking **before** skip/tolerance mutation cases run.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 04d082abcf62c893c2bccf3c462ffbfbb7b46387. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->",
