      "commit": {
        "author": {
          "name": "Jérôme Piquot",
          "email": "jpiquot@itaneo.com",
          "date": "2026-11-04T09:13:21Z"
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Jérôme Piquot",
          "email": "jpiquot@itaneo.com",
          "date": "2026-11-04T09:13:21Z"
        },
        "message": "fix(routing): rebase dispatch lease admission onto an unchanged catalog authority\n\nRouteCatalogAuthority.AcquireAsync now validates the committed catalog\ngeneration outside the state compare-exchange, then re-reads the state and\nappends its dispatch fence only when the epoch and the activation bytes are\nunchanged. Lease-only writers that advance the inventory during validation\nno longer invalidate the admission, a retained lease is recovered after its\nfence is checked, and the lease snapshot uses the identity and coordinates\ncaptured at validation time.\n\nAdds CatalogAdmissionRebaseTests and updates the read-count and stage\ndiagnostics expectations for the extra admission read.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "tree": {
          "sha": "915a870632b338570e054e62ef27fba5d1e5fcb5",
